# Workflow signals from `devkit workflow next`

Read this when `next` prints a line beyond `[STAGE]`, `[UNMET]`, `[CHECK]`, `[NEXT_SKILL]` and `[RETURNS]`. The
`devkit-workflow` skill covers the generic lines (`[DELEGATE]`, `[GATE_PASSED]`, `[STALE_APPROVAL]`, `[BLOCKED]`,
`[PENDING_QUESTION]`, `answer=given`); error lines and advisories carry their own `[FIX]` or `[ACTION]`. This file
adds the spec delivery rules.

## Human gates

For `[WAITING: human gate:<gate>]`, reuse an explicit authorization that covers this exact decision; otherwise ask
once. Record only the authority actually given:

- `plan-intent`: an existing explicit task instruction counts;
  `devkit workflow answer --unit <dir> --request gate:plan-intent --action accept --by user`.
- `plan-accept`: after the Host presents the findings and effects and receives the user's decision,
  `devkit spec proposal accept <slug> --mode accept_only|accept_and_handoff --by user`. `proposal-handoff` can share
  the conversation; each policy stays independent.
- A decline: `devkit workflow answer --unit <dir> --request gate:<gate> --action decline --by user --note "<decision>"`.
{% if execution.environment == "local" %}- `dev-integration`: present the verified report and effects, obtain conversational approval, then run
  `devkit integration integrate` ([policy](../../spec/references/completion.md#policy)).
{% else %}- `dev-integration`: present the verified report and return it to the Host unless a separately authorized CLI/PR
  route exists ([policy](../../spec/references/completion.md#policy)).
{% endif %}
## Other lines

- `[DELEGATE: role=<role> ...]`: delegate through `spec-delegate`.
- `[WAITING: runner ...]` (`lint-ci-clean`, `merged`): still do the stage's `[NEXT_SKILL]` work; once CI, the PR merge
  or the local cumulative check has reported, re-run `next --given <check>`.
- `[BLOCKED: ...]`: the recovery is yours inside the approved scope, the user's when the scope must change.

## Stage ids

- `sdd-session-feature`, `sdd-session-bugfix` and `sdd-overall-refactor` have no unit; `next` does not evaluate them.
- `collect-feedback` is Planning's sweep before `direction-handoff`:
  [run coverage](../../spec-feedback/references/sweep.md#planning-run-coverage).
- `spike` has no exit check, so `[DONE: ... spike]` is not Planning evidence; the `scout` and `challenger` envelopes
  and their `reverify` recorded at `spike` are, at the effort the `spec` skill's `references/planning.md` step 3
  requires.
